    "['monitor session [parameter1] destination interface [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set forwarding-options analyzer SPAN-1 input ingress interface ge-1/0/0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco SPAN (mirroring) configuration command:\\n\\n##\\nset forwarding-options analyzer SPAN-1 input ingress interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset forwarding-options analyzer SPAN-1 output interface ge-1/0/1.0\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper uses \"analyzers\" instead of \"monitor sessions\"\\n2. \"SPAN-1\" is the analyzer name equivalent to session 1\\n3. Juniper requires specifying ingress/egress direction (ingress for RX)\\n4. Juniper requires interface names with \".0\" suffix (ge-1/0/1.0)\\n5. This is actually two commands needed to fully replicate the Cisco functionality', 'trans_template': 'set forwarding-options analyzer SPAN-1 input ingress interface ge-1/0/0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set forwarding-options analyzer SPAN-1 output interface ge-1/0/1.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco SPAN (mirroring) configuration command:\\n\\n##\\nset forwarding-options analyzer SPAN-1 input ingress interface ge-1/0/0.0\\nset forwarding-options analyzer SPAN-1 output interface ge-1/0/1.0\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper uses \"analyzers\" instead of \"monitor sessions\"\\n2. \"SPAN-1\" is the analyzer name equivalent to session 1\\n3. Juniper requires specifying ingress/egress direction (ingress for RX)\\n4. Juniper requires interface names with \".0\" suffix (ge-1/0/1.0)\\n5. This is actually two commands needed to fully replicate the Cisco functionality', 'trans_template': 'set forwarding-options analyzer SPAN-1 output interface ge-1/0/1.0'}]]": 1,
